WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
Observation data should remain connected to mission context.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:07.930
Use consistent file names that include a date, mission identifier, platform or sensor,

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:08.500
and sequence.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.500
Avoid generic names that lose meaning after files move.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:15.450
Preserve available metadata such as capture time, location, altitude estimate,

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:19.000
orientation, device, and camera settings when the mission requires it.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.430
Metadata is useful context but can be incomplete, altered, or imprecise,

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:24.965
so it should not be treated as absolute proof.

00:00:24.965 --> 00:00:28.830
Flight logs and source notes should record objective, crew, equipment, route, weather,

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:31.985
lighting, settings, deviations, and significant events.

00:00:31.985 --> 00:00:36.560
Map references link images to the area of interest and help reviewers understand coverage

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:37.215
and gaps.

00:00:37.215 --> 00:00:39.750
Protect original imagery from accidental editing.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.980
Store working copies, annotations, crops, and processed products separately,

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.000
and document transformations.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.430
Every observation in a report should point to the relevant original or controlled

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:49.145
derivative.

00:00:49.145 --> 00:00:51.450
Storage and access should reflect sensitivity.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:55.985
Imagery may reveal private property, people, infrastructure, or operational details.

00:00:55.985 --> 00:00:59.610
Use approved encrypted storage and transfer where appropriate, restrict access,

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:00.979
and log significant exports.

00:01:00.979 --> 00:01:04.000
Retention should match mission, policy, legal, and evidentiary needs.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.950
Remove unnecessary data through approved processes when the retention period ends.

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:12.130
Good documentation makes analysis repeatable without turning a limited mission into an

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:13.960
indefinite surveillance archive.
